Ladybird shows the console messages of a tab’s same-process iframes in
the tab’s console, along with the top-level document’s. Gecko does the
same: For a window target, its console API listener takes the messages
of each window that WebConsoleUtils.getInnerWindowIDsForFrames() names.
And Blink’s MainThreadDebugger::ContextCreated() puts each frame’s
context in the page’s V8 context group, so V8 reports any frame’s
console calls to the DevTools session of the page.
